> _Reasoning_
> Ah, `start_date` cast to 'date' returns `CarbonImmutable` in Laravel 13? Actually `date` cast returns `Illuminate\Support\Carbon` by default... but here it says CarbonImmutable returned. Hmm. Maybe Laravel 13 changed `date` cast to return CarbonImmutable, or there's a global `Date::use(CarbonImmutable::class)`.
> 
> Let me check AppServiceProvider.
> 
> The error is in the closure at line 66: `fn (Task $task): Carbon => $task->start_date->copy()->startOfDay()`. So `$task->start_date` is CarbonImmutable, and ->copy() returns CarbonImmutable.
> 
> So the return type `: Carbon` is wrong. Let me use `CarbonInterface` instead, or `Illuminate\Support\Carbon`. Let me check AppServiceProvider for Date::use.
