> Standard approach avoiding a11y lint issues: use a `<button>` for the backdrop.
> 
> ```tsx
> <div className="fixed inset-0 z-50 overflow-y-auto">
>     <button
>         type="button"
>         aria-label="Tutup"
>         onClick={onClose}
>         className="fixed inset-0 cursor-default bg-gray-900/50"
>     />
>     <div
>         role="dialog"
>         aria-modal="true"
>         aria-label={title}
>         className={cn(
>             'relative z-10 mx-auto my-6 w-[calc(100%-2rem)] rounded-md bg-white shadow-lg',
>             size === 'lg' ? 'max-w-3xl' : 'max-w-2xl',
>         )}
>     >
>         <header className="flex items-start gap-3 border-b border-gray-200 px-4 py-3">
>             ...
>         </header>
>         <div className="px-4 py-4">{children}</div>
>         {footer ? <footer className="flex justify-end gap-2 border-t border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 px-4 py-3">{footer}</footer> : null}
>     </div>
> </div>
> ```
> 
> Note: `w-[calc(100%-2rem)]` with `mx-auto` centers it. `my-6` gives vertical spacing. On small screens it takes the width minus 2rem. Good.
> 
> For centering vertically when short: `my-6` won't center. It'll be top-aligned with a small margin. That's actually common and avoids the "floating centered modal" look. Hmm, for a normal developer look, top-aligned with margin is fine and more standard for forms. Let me keep `my-6`.
> 
> Actually for a small confirm dialog, top-aligned looks odd. Let me center vertically using flex:
> 
> ```tsx
> <div className="fixed inset-0 z-50 flex min-h-full items-start justify-center overflow-y-auto p-4 sm:items-center">
> ```
> 
> Hmm, but then the backdrop button inside a flex container would be a flex item. `fixed inset-0` takes it out of flow (position fixed), so it won't be a flex item affecting layout. Good — `position: fixed` elements are removed from normal flow, so flex won't lay them out. 
> 
> So:
> ```tsx
> <div className="fixed inset-0 z-50 flex overflow-y-auto p-4">
>     <button ... className="fixed inset-0 cursor-default bg-gray-900/50" />
>     <div className="relative z-10 m-auto w-full max-w-2xl rounded-md bg-white shadow-lg">...</div>
> </div>
> ```
> `m-auto` inside a flex container centers the dialog both ways, and with `overflow-y-auto` on the parent, a tall dialog scrolls. This is a very standard pattern. 
