> Note: with `grid-cols-2` on mobile and 5 items, the last item leaves an empty cell — the bg-gray-200 would show as an empty gray cell. Hmm, that's a visual flaw. With 5 items in 2 columns: rows = 3, last row has 1 item + 1 empty cell showing gray. Ugly.
> 
> Fix: use a different approach — `divide-x`/`divide-y` won't handle wrapping nicely either.
> 
> Alternative: give each cell its own border and use negative margins... Simpler: on mobile use `grid-cols-1` (5 stacked rows) with borders between, and on larger screens use the gap-px trick. Still the empty-cell problem on `sm:grid-cols-3` (5 items → 1 empty cell in row 2).
> 
> Cleanest: avoid the divider trick. Use individual bordered cards in a responsive grid:
