The milestone diamond used `border-amber-700` (dark amber); the spec says *"belah ketupat warna emas/hitam"*. Changed to `border-gray-900`. Because source changed, I re-ran **every** gate and suite afterward rather than reusing earlier results.

## Spec conformance, artifact by artifact

**Schema** (`SHOW COLUMNS` on `ganttflow_db.tasks`): `id` bigint PRI · `wbs_code` varchar · `name` varchar · `task_type` enum(`regular`,`summary`,`milestone`) · `start_date`/`end_date` date · `duration_days` int · `progress` tinyint unsigned (0–100) · `priority` enum(`Low`,`Normal`,`High`,`Critical`) · `parent_id`/`predecessor_id` bigint nullable FK · `dependency_type` enum(`FS`,`SS`,`FF`,`SF`) default `FS` · `lag_days` int · `resource_names` varchar nullable · `status` enum(`Not Started`,`In Progress`,`Completed`) — all 15 requested columns present with the requested types.

**UI contract (11/11):** grid columns exactly `WBS | Nama Tugas | Durasi | Mulai | Selesai | Dep. | % | Resources`; every row the same fixed height `34px`; dependency cells match `1.1FS`, `2.1SS+1d`; regular bar fill = its % (100% fill on 100% progress) with a resize handle; summary = 3-part black bracket (7px); milestone = `45deg` gold diamond 21×21 with dark outline (fill L=0.828, stroke L=0.21); all 12 toolbar/navbar controls present; "Tentang" opens the popup (title `Tentang GanttFlow`) and Escape closes it; PERT renders 16 nodes each showing ES/EF/LS/LF.

**Gates, each with its real exit code: `[0]`** — `php artisan test` (35 passed), `pint --test`, `phpstan` level 7, `types:check`, `check`, `build`.

**Browser, against the production build:** `[0]` full UI **35/35**, `[0]` contract **11/11**, `[0]` MySQL round-trip **5/5** (raw SQL INSERT → appears in grid *and* timeline; DELETE → disappears; plus drag → `2026-10-19`, resize → `2d→6d`, rename all persisted).

## Checks that failed and how they were fixed

Six failures were **my own assertions being wrong, not app defects**, and I corrected the assertions rather than loosening them: a sync IIFE containing `await`, a missing await after closing the dialog, measuring the progress fill against the bar's border-box instead of `clientWidth`, reading `transform` when Tailwind v4 sets the standalone `rotate` property, a search string colliding with the existing task "…Verifikasi Berkas", and a `\\d` regex written as `\\d`. The two real app defects found earlier in this work remain fixed and covered: the SF slack error (replaced with sensitivity-based float) and 3 connector/bar crossings (now 0).

